HALLYU — COMPLETE UI/UX + MOTION IMPLEMENTATION BRIEF

Product: Hallyu
Tagline: Where Fandoms Meet.
Platform: Mobile — Expo / React Native
Product type: Social entertainment community
Core worlds: K-Dramas · C-Dramas · Anime · Hollywood

Goal

Build Hallyu as a premium, cinematic social entertainment platform, not a database, not a streaming clone, and not a generic social-media feed.

Hallyu brings entertainment fandoms into one community.

Users discover movies, series, anime, people, creators and communities, then discuss, react, recommend, save and share what they love.

The interface should feel:

Cinematic · Social · Premium · Dark · Fast · Immersive · Human

---

0. NORTH STAR

Hallyu should feel like entering a private entertainment world where the content and the people around it exist together.

The central idea:

«Discover what you love. Find people who love it too.»

The four initial entertainment worlds are:

🇰🇷 K-Dramas

🇨🇳 C-Dramas

🇯🇵 Anime

🇺🇸 Hollywood

These are NOT four separate applications.

They are four major fandom worlds inside one Hallyu ecosystem.

Users can belong to one, several, or all four.

Core product loop

Discover → React → Discuss → Follow → Create → Discover

The community is not an extra feature attached to entertainment discovery.

The community IS the product.

Anti-goals

Do NOT make Hallyu:

- A Netflix clone
- A TikTok clone
- A Reddit clone
- An IMDb clone
- A Letterboxd clone
- A generic social-media app
- A database with comments attached
- A generic AI-looking interface
- Purple-gradient "AI startup" UI
- An overloaded dashboard
- Excessively glassy
- Visually noisy

